    "bbox": [
      185.85,
      226.97,
      377.85,
      250.31
    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDUREACT, NO. 15 OF 1979",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      262.97,
      401.91,
      286.31
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      298.97,
      401.88,
      322.31
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Code of CriminalProcedure (Amendment) Act, No. of 2019.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      334.97,
      401.89,
      382.31
    ],
    "text": "2.The following new section is hereby insertedimmediately after section 144 of the Code of CriminalProcedure Act, No.15 of 1979 and shall have effect as section144A of that Act:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      216.81,
      394.97,
      401.88,
      490.31
    ],
    "text": "144A. (1) The Magistrate may, at hisdiscretion, dispense with the personalattendance of a suspect or accused in court, inrespect of whom criminal proceedings havebeen instituted before such Magistrate, forextending the period of detention or for anyother purpose, at the end of each detentionperiod, or on each trial date.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      216.81,
      502.97,
      401.91,
      598.31
    ],
    "text": "(2) The personal attendance of the suspector accused may be so dispensed with, on anapplication made by the relevant person, asspecified in subsection (3), if the Magistrate issatisfied that the personal attendance of suchsuspect or accused in court may be dispensedwith, on any one or more of the groundsspecified in subsection (4).",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      216.81,
      610.97,
      401.86,
      646.31
    ],
    "text": "(3) An application under subsection (2), inrespect of a suspect or accused, shall be madeby \u2013",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      234.57,
      658.97,
      356.86,
      670.31
    ],
    "text": "(a)the Attorney General; or",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      395.83,
      209.86,
      472.1
    ],
    "text": "\u201cPersonalattendance ofthe suspect oraccused maybe dispensedwith, underspecialcircumstances.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      166.97,
      363.07,
      178.31
    ],
    "text": "Code of Criminal Procedure (Amendment)2",
    "fonts": [
      "Times,Italic",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
